 "requested_at": "2026-11-12T19:52:28.729039Z",
 "text": "The clause is not enforceable. Section 106 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (S.O. 2006, c. 17) prohibits a landlord from requiring a tenant to give a post-dated cheque or other negotiable instrument as security or as a condition of the tenancy, and a signed blank cheque kept as security falls within that prohibition. The tenant also cannot waive the protection by agreement (s. 4), so the clause is void even though the tenant signed it.\n\nI haven't checked the current consolidated text of the Act, so confirm the wording of s. 106 before relying on it. The Landlord and Tenant Board or a community legal clinic can also confirm the position.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
